Z||000000||GT-maniac||05-21-2000||11:27 AM||||I've read much about putting brakes from other cars on Fieros and was wondering if it's possible to install the 88 fiero's braking system on earlier models ? Or are they just too different ? The brakes on the 88's look to be superior with their vented discs and would hopefully allow me to retain the emergency brake. I have to have the e-brake working to get the car insured where I live.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Fformula88||05-21-2000||09:13 PM||||I dunno if you can swap the brakes... but I don't think you will gain much by putting 88 brakes on your Fiero.  I really don't notice much of a difference in the stopping of my 88 Formula and my dads 87 Coupe.  Besides... parts for the 88's are hard to find and WAY TOO expesnive for what they are worth.  If you cannot do a different swap, I'd just keep what you have.  Maybe get some performance pads or something for them.  Good luck!||||reg||1
Z||000002||sid1200||05-22-2000||04:05 AM||||your 88 brakes might be shot, my 88 GT and my friends 88 GT stops way better than his 87 GT, both with new brakes, night and day difference.<P>88 brakes are larger and vented. 10.5 inch discs vs. 9.5 for the earlier models.||||reg||1
